{%- comment -%}
  YMAL — the add to cart popup's source list.

  Fetched as /products/<handle>?view=ymal-popup. Returns JSON and nothing else:

    {"handles": ["ninth", "tenth", ...], "styles": ["NINTH STYLE", ...]}

  DELIBERATELY SKIPS THE FIRST 8. Those are what the YMAL row on the product
  page already showed, and the shopper has just walked past them on the way to
  adding this product. The popup's job is to widen the choice, not to repeat
  the row one scroll later - so it offers from position 9 onward.

  Counted in ELIGIBLE products, the same ones the row would render: not this
  product, available, ymal.eligible, no *SALE*. A skipped product does not use
  up one of the eight, or the popup would start somewhere different from where
  the row ended.

  The pool is 30 deep, so there is room: 12 are returned, and the script
  shuffles them and shows 3.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% layout none %}
{%- liquid
  assign ymal_skip = 8
  assign ymal_limit = 12
  assign ymal_seen = 0
  assign ymal_count = 0
  assign ymal_handles = ''
  assign ymal_styles = ''

  for ymal_item in product.metafields.ymal.featured.value
    if ymal_count >= ymal_limit
      break
    endif
    if ymal_item.id == product.id
      continue
    endif
    unless ymal_item.available
      continue
    endunless
    unless ymal_item.metafields.ymal.eligible.value
      continue
    endunless
    if ymal_item.title contains '*SALE*'
      continue
    endif

    assign ymal_seen = ymal_seen | plus: 1
    if ymal_seen <= ymal_skip
      continue
    endif

    if ymal_count > 0
      assign ymal_handles = ymal_handles | append: ','
      assign ymal_styles = ymal_styles | append: ','
    endif
    assign ymal_handle_json = ymal_item.handle | json
    assign ymal_style_json = ymal_item.title | strip | upcase | json
    assign ymal_handles = ymal_handles | append: ymal_handle_json
    assign ymal_styles = ymal_styles | append: ymal_style_json
    assign ymal_count = ymal_count | plus: 1
  endfor
-%}
{"handles": [{{ ymal_handles }}], "styles": [{{ ymal_styles }}]}
